# The build context is this whole repository, where the image needs only what
# `pip install .` reads. What is listed here is regenerated, private, or has no
# business in a wheel.
#
# (!!) An entry here that setuptools needs is a package installed without its
# data, and it shows up as a rule file missing at runtime rather than as a
# build failure. `pyproject.toml`, the packages it names and their package-data
# have to stay.
.git
.github
.venv
.vscode
build
madmp_core.egg-info
**/__pycache__
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
tests
doc.md
